. *----------------------------------------------------- eastbound: no threshol
> d
. * Same axes, same scale, same threshold strip, and now a fitted line of its o
> wn.
. *
. * Extending the window to the present is what made drawing it defensible. On 
> the
. * shorter window the below-kink slope rested on two discount months; it now
. * rests on nine, and the earlier flat claim - that this leg shows no price
. * response at all - was too strong. What survives is weaker and the panel say
> s
. * so in figures rather than in adjectives: the threshold interval spans zero,
. * the straight-line R-squared is 0.01, and the correlation is -0.11 on 43
. * months. The line is drawn; the reader is told not to lean on it.
. twoway ///
>   `BAND' ///
>   (scatter us_to_che_t excess_usd if ishinge == 0 & !grp, ///
>       `SCAT' mcolor("`GREY'%60")) ///
